lots.description:
The new service will be a 3 step (tier) integrated service, combining universal preventative support, a targeted group and one to one programme. The service will be delivered both face to face and online across the county, with a proportionate universalism approach used to address key obesity related health inequalities. Additional information: This is a Provider Selection Regime (PSR) Contract Notice. The awarding of this contract is subject to the Health Care Services (Provider Selection Regime) Regulations 2023. For the avoidance of doubt, the provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 do not apply to this award. 
1. Visit https://sell2.in-tend.co.uk/cambridgeshire/home to access the In-Tend supplier portal;
2. Register/log-in and access the Cambridgeshire County Council company portal;
3. Search for current tender opportunities - this procurement is named "26055 Child Weight Management";
4. Express interest to get access to the tender documents;
5. Opt-in to view the ITT questionnaire;
6. Complete questionnaire, add mandatory documents and any other relevant documents as part of your tender return;
7. Click "submit return" to submit your ITT response.
Relative Importance of Key Criteria:
1) 35% Quality and Innovation
2) 15% Integration, collaboration and service sustainability 
3) 15% Improving access, reducing health inequalities and facilitating choice 
4) 5% Social Value
5) 30% Value

criteria.description:
Bidders must demonstrate that they have the technical and professional capability, capacity and experience necessary to successfully implement, transition and support the services required under this contract.
As a minimum, bidders will be expected to demonstrate:
relevant and recent experience of successfully implementing and supporting cloud-based corporate telephony and Contact Centre as a Service (CCaaS) solutions of comparable scale, scope and complexity;
experience of implementing omnichannel contact centre capabilities incorporating voice and digital channels, intelligent routing, workforce management, interaction recording, quality management, reporting and analytics;
experience and capability in the implementation and support of artificial intelligence, automation and advanced interaction analytics, including capabilities such as speech-to-text transcription, sentiment and topic analysis, automated summarisation, conversational analytics, advisor assistance, automated quality management and conversational AI;
appropriate technical resources, skills, implementation methodologies, project management and service management capabilities to design, configure, integrate, migrate, test, transition and support the proposed solution;
experience of integrating CCaaS solutions with enterprise applications, Microsoft technologies, CRM and line-of-business systems, data and reporting platforms, knowledge services and payment services using appropriate APIs and integration technologies;
appropriate information security, cyber security, data protection, business continuity and disaster recovery arrangements applicable to the delivery of the services;
capability to securely process and manage customer interactions, recordings, transcripts and other personal or sensitive information, including appropriate controls relating to AI-enabled processing;
appropriate arrangements for the management of subcontractors and third-party technology providers forming part of the proposed solution; and
sufficient suitably qualified and experienced personnel and resources to deliver the implementation and provide ongoing support throughout the contract term.
Bidders may be required to provide details of relevant contracts delivered during the previous three years, including client references, together with evidence of appropriate technical capability, certifications, accreditations and resources.
Where a bidder relies upon the technical or professional capacity of another organisation, the bidder must demonstrate that the necessary resources will be available for the delivery of the contract.
Further details of the minimum selection requirements, evidence requirements and any mandatory technical criteria are set out in the procurement documents.
